+<path d="M980,254 C980,300 900,340 840,355" class="ar s"/><text x="905" y="320" class="m">insert, own tx</text>
+</svg>
+<p class="legend">Filter order matters: the rate limiter runs before authentication so API-key guessing is throttled too. Every error, from a filter or a controller, is RFC 9457 Problem Details with a request id.</p>
+
+<h2><span class="n">04</span> The two flows that matter</h2>
+<div class="grid g2">
+<div>
+<h3>Create: POST /api/v1/links</h3>
+<div class="lane">
+<div>1 filters</div><div>Request id assigned. Body over 16 KiB → 413. Bucket empty → 429. Bad key → 401 with WWW-Authenticate.</div>
+<div>2 validate</div><div>Absolute http/https, host present, no user info, ≤ 2048 chars, host not loopback, private, link-local, or metadata. Violations → 400 with <code>errors[]</code>.</div>
+<div>3 alias?</div><div>If given: regex, reserved list, fast <code>existsByCode</code> → 409 if taken.</div>
+<div>4 allocate</div><div>Loop ≤ 5: draw a code (or use the alias) → <code>LinkAllocator.insert</code> in <em>its own transaction</em>. Unique violation on <code>uk_links_code</code>: random code → retry; alias → 409.</div>
+<div>5 respond</div><div>201, <code>Location: /api/v1/links/{code}</code>, body with shortUrl derived from the request host unless <code>app.base-url</code> is set.</div>
+</div>
+</div>
+<div>
+<h3>Redirect: GET /{code}</h3>
+<div class="lane">
+<div>1 route</div><div>Path pattern <code>{code:[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,32}}</code>, so favicon and dotfiles never reach the database.</div>
+<div>2 lookup</div><div>One indexed read by code. Missing → 404. Expired → 410. Both <code>Cache-Control: no-store</code>.</div>
+<div>3 hand off</div><div>Build immutable <code>ClickRecorded(linkId, now, requestId)</code> on the request thread; offer it to the bounded queue. Full queue → drop and count.</div>
+<div>4 respond</div><div>302 with <code>Location</code> and explicit <code>no-store</code>. HEAD resolves but is not counted.</div>
+<div>5 async</div><div>Executor thread inserts one row in its own transaction; failures are caught and counted, never propagated.</div>
+</div>
+</div>
+</div>
+
+<h2><span class="n">05</span> Short-code algorithm and why</h2>
+<div class="grid g2">
+<div class="card">
+<h4>Chosen: random 7-character Base62, uniqueness by the database, bounded retry</h4>
+<div class="math">alphabet = [0-9A-Za-z]  (62 symbols, URL-safe, no escaping)<br>code = 7 × SecureRandom.nextInt(62)<br>keyspace = 62^7 = 3,521,614,606,208 ≈ 3.5 × 10^12<br>birthday bound: E[collisions] ≈ n² / (2 × 62^7)<br>n = 1,000,000 → ≈ 0.14 expected collisions<br>n = 10,000,000 → ≈ 14 expected collisions<br>at 1,000 new links/s the keyspace lasts ≈ 111 years</div>
+<ul>
+<li>Non-enumerable by construction. Sequential codes can be scanned; the 2016 "Gone in Six Characters" study exposed private cloud documents that way.</li>
+<li>No extra infrastructure. The INSERT itself enforces uniqueness through the unique index; there is no separate lookup round trip.</li>
+<li>Collisions are rare but handled, never assumed away: each attempt is its own transaction so a violation cannot poison the request's transaction, and a lost race on a custom alias maps to 409 rather than a retry.</li>
+<li>SecureRandom is cryptographically strong and thread-safe; one shared instance.</li>
+</ul>
+</div>
+<div class="card">
+<h4>Alternatives and when they win</h4>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Approach</th><th>Pros</th><th>Why not here</th></tr>
+<tr><td>Base62(counter)</td><td>No collisions; shortest codes; decodable ids; the Redis INCR design with block reservation scales writes across regions</td><td>Enumerable unless obfuscated, and XOR or Hashids obfuscation is reversible; needs Redis; the right switch when many writers need decodable ids</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Hash(URL)</td><td>Deterministic; dedupes repeat URLs</td><td>Collides and must still be resolved; determinism leaks that two users shortened the same URL unless salted</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Snowflake</td><td>Uncoordinated, time-sortable</td><td>Encodes to about 11 Base62 chars and leaks creation time and worker id; solves distribution, not shortness</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Key generation service</td><td>Pre-generated blocks, zero collisions</td><td>A second service for a single node; listed as the scaling step</td></tr>
+</table>
+</div>
+</div>
+
+<h2><span class="n">06</span> Data model and migrations</h2>
+<div class="grid g3">
+<div class="card"><h4>links (V1, greenfield)</h4>
+<table><tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th></tr>
+<tr><td>id</td><td>BIGINT identity, PK</td></tr><tr><td>code</td><td>VARCHAR(32), <code>uk_links_code</code> UNIQUE</td></tr><tr><td>original_url</td><td>VARCHAR(2048)</td></tr><tr><td>created_at</td><td>TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE</td></tr><tr><td>expires_at</td><td>TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE, nullable, <strong>V2 brownfield</strong></td></tr></table></div>
+<div class="card"><h4>click_events (V1)</h4>
+<table><tr><th>Column</th><th>Type</th></tr>
+<tr><td>id</td><td>BIGINT identity, PK</td></tr><tr><td>link_id</td><td>BIGINT, FK → links ON DELETE CASCADE</td></tr><tr><td>occurred_at</td><td>TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2">index <code>(link_id, occurred_at)</code> serves every stats query<br>V3 only if the ambiguous clarification decides so</td></tr></table></div>
+<div class="card"><h4>Rules</h4>
+<ul><li>Instant fields map to TIMESTAMP_UTC in Hibernate 7, hence time-zone columns, or startup validation fails.</li><li>One ALTER per column: H2 and PostgreSQL disagree on the multi-column form.</li><li>click_events.link_id is a plain column, so a click is one INSERT with no SELECT.</li><li>No IP, no raw user agent, ever.</li><li>Stats = one aggregate query: count, two conditional sums, max.</li></ul></div>
+</div>
+
+<h2><span class="n">07</span> Key decisions</h2>
+<table>
+<tr><th>ADR</th><th>Decision</th><th>Rejected</th><th>Deciding factor</th></tr>
+<tr><td>0001</td><td>Java 21, Spring Boot 4.1.1, Maven wrapper</td><td>Boot 3.5, Java 25, Gradle</td><td>Role requires Java; 4.1.x supported to mid-2027; reviewers' JDK</td></tr>
+<tr><td>0002</td><td>H2 file + Flyway + validate</td><td>PostgreSQL via Docker</td><td>No Docker or admin on reviewer laptops; schema change control</td></tr>
+<tr><td>0003</td><td>Random Base62 with per-attempt transactions</td><td>Counter, hash, Snowflake</td><td>Non-enumerable, no infrastructure, correctness under races</td></tr>
+<tr><td>0004</td><td>302 + no-store</td><td>301</td><td>301 is heuristically cacheable; clicks and expiry would be lost</td></tr>
+<tr><td>0005</td><td>Events table, async insert</td><td>Counter column; synchronous insert</td><td>Hot-row serialisation; redirect isolation</td></tr>
+<tr><td>0006</td><td>No IP or raw user agent</td><td>Truncated IP, salted hash</td><td>Regulated-firm privacy posture</td></tr>
+<tr><td>0007</td><td>Spring Security, API key, limiter before auth</td><td>Bare filter</td><td>Expected by enterprise reviewers; throttles key guessing</td></tr>
+<tr><td>0008</td><td>Process as code with a JUnit validator module</td><td>Markdown only; mini platform</td><td>Checkable traceability, product code untouched</td></tr>
+<tr><td>0009</td><td>Task trailer in commits, AI provenance in the ledger</td><td>Assisted-by trailers</td><td>Repository convention; ledger is the richer record</td></tr>
+</table>
+<p class="legend">Smaller decisions: platform threads because the H2 driver pins virtual threads on Java 21 · expired rows kept, no sweeper · hard delete with the alias-reclaim risk recorded · no server-side fetch of targets · no rollups.</p>
+
+<h2><span class="n">08</span> Security, reliability, observability</h2>
+<div class="grid g3">
+<div class="card"><h4>Security</h4><ul><li>Redirect only to the stored, pre-validated URL</li><li>Internal-host laundering blocked at create</li><li>API key, constant-time compare, prod fails fast without it</li><li>Rate limit before auth; body size cap; URL length cap</li><li>Log sanitiser for user-controlled values</li><li>Headers: nosniff, DENY, no-referrer, CSP on Swagger only</li><li>SpotBugs + FindSecBugs, gitleaks, Dependabot</li></ul></div>
+<div class="card"><h4>Reliability</h4><ul><li>One transaction per allocation attempt</li><li>Bounded click executor, drop-and-count, 10 s drain on shutdown</li><li>503 + Retry-After within 2 s when the database is unavailable</li><li>Graceful shutdown, readiness and liveness probes</li><li>Problem Details from every layer, identical shape</li></ul></div>
+<div class="card"><h4>Observability</h4><ul><li>X-Request-Id bounded and echoed; in logs and error bodies</li><li>Counters: links.created, redirects{outcome}, clicks.dropped</li><li>Actuator health with database indicator; build info</li><li>Prometheus endpoint; structured JSON logs in prod</li></ul></div>
+</div>
+
+<h2><span class="n">09</span> Scaling path</h2>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Concern</th><th>Prototype</th><th>Next</th><th>Later</th></tr>
+<tr><td>Database</td><td>H2 file</td><td>PostgreSQL, same SQL and migrations</td><td>Read replicas</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Hot lookups</td><td>Indexed read</td><td>Caffeine cache, evict on delete and expiry</td><td>Redis provider, same @Cacheable code</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Clicks</td><td>Async insert, one aggregate query</td><td>Hourly rollups with a watermark</td><td>Queue and streaming aggregation</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Rate limit</td><td>In-process Bucket4j</td><td>Bucket4j on Redis</td><td>Edge limiting</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Codes</td><td>Random + retry</td><td>Pre-generated key blocks or an obfuscated counter</td><td>Key generation service</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Instances</td><td>One</td><td>Stateless nodes behind a load balancer, trusted-proxy config</td><td>Multi-region</td></tr>
+</table>
+
+<h2><span class="n">10</span> Deployment for the reviewer</h2>
+<div class="grid g2">
+<div class="card"><h4>What they need</h4><ul><li>JDK 21 (zip install, no admin)</li><li>Internet to Maven Central once; proxy and truststore notes in README</li><li>Git or Download ZIP</li></ul></div>
+<div class="card"><h4>What they run</h4><ul><li><code>.\mvnw.cmd -pl url-shortener spring-boot:run</code></li><li>Swagger UI at <code>/swagger-ui.html</code>, Authorize with the dev key</li><li><code>.\mvnw.cmd verify</code> runs every gate and the traceability check</li></ul></div>
+</div>
+
