+# R-01: Greenfield requirement record
+
+## Title
+
+"Build a URL shortener service with core APIs, analytics, and reliability features"
+
+## Source
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Origin | The assignment brief, greenfield scenario |
+| Design sections | docs/design/2026-10-12-system-design.md#1.2, #1.3, #1.5, #3, #6.1 |
+| Status | normalized |
+| Normalized on | 2026-10-12 |
+
+## Normalized problem statement
+
+Deliver a single-node HTTP service that creates short links for validated absolute http or https URLs, redirects on `GET /{code}` with 302 and `Cache-Control: no-store`, records each click off the request thread, and reports per-link totals over all time, 24 hours, and 7 days. Metadata, stats, and delete sit behind one API key on `/api/v1`. Reliability means validation, rate limiting, request size limits, RFC 9457 Problem Details, correlation ids, isolated analytics, graceful shutdown, and 503 with `Retry-After` when the database is unavailable. The whole thing builds and runs on a clean Windows or Linux machine with JDK 21 and no other installs, and every AI-assisted change is traceable through the harness.
+
+## Functional requirements covered
+
+- FR-01 to FR-04: create, custom alias, alias race to 409, URL validation (T-003, T-004)
+- FR-05 to FR-07: redirect, 404 without lookup for malformed codes, asynchronous click recording (T-005)
+- FR-08, FR-09: stats, metadata, delete (T-006)
+- FR-10, FR-11: API key on `/api/v1/**`, create rate limit (T-007)
+- FR-12: actuator endpoints, OpenAPI drift gate, Swagger UI with Authorize (T-008, T-009)
+
+## Non-functional requirements covered
+
+- NFR-01 portability and NFR-08, NFR-09 gates: T-000, T-001; proven by CI on both operating systems
+- NFR-02 redirect latency smoke and NFR-03, NFR-04 analytics isolation and drain: T-005, T-009
+- NFR-05 security controls and NFR-07 correlation and counters: T-003, T-005, T-007
+- NFR-06 privacy and NFR-10 schema change safety: T-002
+- NFR-11 process auditability: T-000 harness skeleton, T-010 review, every task's ledger entry
+
+## Ambiguities identified and reading adopted
+
+| Ambiguity | Reading adopted | Where decided |
+|---|---|---|
+| "Core APIs" | The table in section 3.3: create, redirect, HEAD, metadata, stats, delete, actuator, OpenAPI | #3.3 |
+| "Analytics" | Per-click events with total, 24 hour, 7 day counts and last click; no attribution, deferred to R-03 | #1.5, FR-08 |
+| "Reliability features" | The list in section 1.5: health, graceful shutdown, validation, rate and size limits, Problem Details, correlation ids, async analytics, 503 with Retry-After | #1.5 |
+| Redirect status | 302 with no-store so every click reaches the server; 301 rejected as cacheable | ADR 0004 |
+| Expiry | Not part of this requirement; delivered by R-02 so the brownfield change is real | #3.5 |
+| "Runnable end-to-end" | One command runs the service; harness checks run inside the same `mvnw verify` | #1.5 |
+
+## Assumptions
+
+- Single node with embedded H2 in file mode; reviewers have no Docker or admin rights (#1.4).
+- Read to write ratio around 10:1, so the redirect path stays minimal and analytics asynchronous.
+- One shared API key for a prototype; per-user ownership is a listed limitation.
+- Reviewers may run on plain HTTP, so HSTS does not appear locally.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- User accounts, per-user ownership, audit of who deleted what.
+- Link expiry (R-02) and click attribution (R-03).
+- Distributed cache, queue, key generation service, rollup tables; scaling path documented only.
+- Server-side fetching of target URLs; idempotency keys; load testing; Docker image.
+
+## Tasks
+
+T-000 toolchain and harness skeleton; T-001 gates and CI; T-002 schema V1; T-003 generator, validator, reserved words, sanitiser; T-004 create; T-005 redirect and click recording; T-006 metadata, stats, delete; T-007 security and rate limiting; T-008 OpenAPI; T-009 integration tests, perf smoke, README, ADRs, scenario evidence; T-010 fresh-context review.
+
+## Validation
+
+- `mvnw verify` green on `windows-latest` and `ubuntu-latest`, including the perf profile on Ubuntu.
+- Every acceptance test named in section 1.2 rows FR-01 to FR-12 passes in the default build.
+- Manual Swagger UI check with the Authorize button recorded with a date in docs/scenarios/greenfield.md.
+- Fresh-clone check from an empty local repository passes and is recorded.
+- harness-check reports zero violations; T-010 produces the defect-candidate list that feeds T-105.
