+id: T-002
+title: Schema V1, entities, repositories, test meta-annotation, migration proof
+requirement: R-01
+activities: [implement, test-gen]
+impact: high
+impact_reasons: [schema]
+status: todo
+depends_on: [T-001]
+intent: >
+  Create the minimal greenfield schema through Flyway V1, the Link and ClickEvent entities, the two
+  Spring Data repositories, and the single test-profile meta-annotation, then prove the migration
+  with a data slice test. The schema is deliberately minimal so the brownfield scenario requires a
+  real migration later.
+constraints:
+  - "SQL in the subset accepted by both H2 in PostgreSQL mode and PostgreSQL; identity columns declared explicitly"
+  - "Columns are TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE and entity fields are Instant so ddl-auto=validate passes under Hibernate 7"
+  - "Constraint and index names exactly uk_links_code, fk_click_events_link, ix_click_events_link_time"
+  - "ClickEvent.linkId is a plain Long column; Link has no collection of events; cascade delete lives in the database"
+  - "Link.equals and hashCode use code; toString excludes original_url"
+  - "No column for IP address or user agent (ADR 0006)"
+  - "Every test carries the single @ActiveProfiles(test) meta-annotation; the test profile uses in-memory H2 in PostgreSQL mode"
+acceptance_criteria:
+  - "WHEN the application starts under any profile THE SYSTEM SHALL apply V1 and pass ddl-auto=validate [NFR-10]"
+  - "WHEN MigrationTest runs under the test profile THE SYSTEM SHALL create links and click_events with the named unique constraint, foreign key with cascade, and index [NFR-10]"
+  - "WHILE the schema exists THE SYSTEM SHALL contain no column holding an IP address or a user-agent string [NFR-06]"
+  - "WHEN a Link is rendered through toString THE SYSTEM SHALL omit original_url [NFR-05]"
+  - "WHEN ClickEventRepository saves an event THE SYSTEM SHALL issue one INSERT with no preceding SELECT [FR-07]"
