+id: T-004
+title: Create link endpoint with per-attempt allocation and Problem Details
+requirement: R-01
+activities: [implement]
+impact: normal
+impact_reasons: []
+status: todo
+depends_on: [T-002, T-003]
+intent: >
+  Expose POST /api/v1/links so clients create short links from validated URLs, with the allocation
+  loop outside the transaction and one transaction per insert attempt. This task also introduces
+  the single error mechanism, ApiExceptionHandler plus ProblemWriter, and the request size filter,
+  so every later endpoint reuses them.
+constraints:
+  - "LinkService.create is not transactional; LinkAllocator.insert is @Transactional on a separate bean, one attempt per transaction, at most five attempts"
+  - "DataIntegrityViolationException is caught outside the proxy and the constraint name uk_links_code is checked; random collision retries, custom alias maps to 409; existsByCode is the fast path"
+  - "All errors are RFC 9457 Problem Details through ApiExceptionHandler extending ResponseEntityExceptionHandler and the shared ProblemWriter; every body carries requestId and timestamp"
+  - "DTOs are records with boxed types and @NotNull; application/json only, otherwise 415"
+  - "RequestSizeFilter rejects bodies over 16 KiB on /api/v1/** with 413 and wraps chunked bodies with a counting stream"
+  - "shortUrl comes from app.base-url when set, otherwise from the request scheme, host, and port"
+  - "No new dependencies"
+acceptance_criteria:
+  - "WHEN a client POSTs a valid absolute http or https URL as JSON THE SYSTEM SHALL create a link with a unique 7-character Base62 code and respond 201 with Location and the link body [FR-01]"
+  - "WHEN a client supplies a custom alias matching ^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,32}$ that is not reserved and not taken THE SYSTEM SHALL use it as the code [FR-02]"
